/*
 ==============================================================================
  AEGIS RIDE : SMART VEHICLE SAFETY & ROAD CONDITION TELEMETRY
  BREADBOARD DEMO BUILD (v4.1)          Target: ESP32 Dev Module / NodeMCU-32S
  No external libraries needed.

  Wiring:
   MPU-6050  : VCC 3.3V, GND, SCL->22, SDA->21
   OLED 0x3C : VDD 3.3V, GND, SCK->22, SDA->21
   NEO-6M GPS: VCC->VIN(5V), GND, TX->GPIO16 (ESP32 RX2), RX->GPIO17 (ESP32 TX2)
   Buzzer    : (+)->GPIO25, (-)->GND
   Button    : GPIO4 <-> GND (internal pull-up & capacitive touch)
               * NOTE: Changed from GPIO15 to GPIO4. GPIO15 is an ESP32 strapping
                 pin with an onboard pull-down resistor on many dev boards,
                 causing buttons to stay LOW.
                 GPIO4 also supports Capacitive Touch! If you touch the GPIO4 wire
                 with your finger, it triggers the button.
                 If you still wish to use GPIO15, change PIN_BUTTON to 15 below.
   Tactile Switch Connection:
     Connect DIAGONALLY OPPOSITE pins across the tactile switch between GPIO4
     and GND. (Do NOT connect adjacent pins on the same side).

  BUTTON CONTROLS:
   - 1 CLICK (Single Click): See LAST EVENT on OLED
   - 2 CLICKS (Double Click): See RECENT LOG, COUNTS & STATUS on OLED
   - 3 CLICKS (Triple Click): Start 15-SECOND SOS COUNTDOWN with warning beeps
   - PRESS DURING COUNTDOWN: IMMEDIATELY TURNS OFF the alarm (Rider safe - No SOS)
   - PRESS AFTER SOS DISPATCH: Dismisses alert & re-arms the system

  ROAD TELEMETRY & FORCE THRESHOLDS:
   - POTHOLE: MINOR = 1.50 G | MEDIUM = 2.20 G | SEVERE = 3.20 G
   - SPEED BREAKER / BUMP: Tilt >= 25 deg held for 0.4s
   - CRASH: Impact >= 4.00 G AND Tilt >= 45 deg within 2.5s
            -> Starts 15-second countdown. Press button to turn off!

  NETWORK LIMITATION:
   - Phone connected ONLY to this ESP32 access point = local dashboard works.
   - WhatsApp needs the ESP32 to ALSO join an internet-enabled router/SECOND hotspot.
   - The ESP32 AP cannot pass the phone's mobile data back to the ESP32 by itself.

  REMOTE EMERGENCY SOS OPTIONS (Wi-Fi & Bluetooth):
   1. WI-FI EMERGENCY WEB DASHBOARD (No App Needed!):
      - Connect smartphone to Wi-Fi: "AEGIS-RIDE-SAFETY" (Password: 12345678)
      - Open browser to: http://192.168.4.1
      - Tap the BIG RED "TRIGGER SOS" button or GREEN "CANCEL" button!
      - View live telemetry and Google Maps location link.
   2. BLUETOOTH SERIAL ("AEGIS-RIDE-SOS"):
      - Pair with phone (Serial Bluetooth Terminal app).
      - Send "sos", "cancel", "info", "status", "cal".
      - When crash occurs or SOS triggers, emergency text + Google Maps link
        is sent directly over Bluetooth to the paired phone.
   3. TELEGRAM AUTO-DISPATCH:
      - Uses only TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID; no CallMeBot needed.

  Arduino IDE Settings:
   - Board: "ESP32 Dev Module"
   - Partition Scheme: "Huge APP (3MB No OTA/1MB SPIFFS)" or "No OTA (2MB APP/2MB SPIFFS)"
 ==============================================================================
*/

